<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Settings - Account Portal (Vulnerable)</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('_nav') %>
  <main class="container">
    <h1>Account settings</h1>
    <% if (success) { %><div class="alert alert-success"><%= success %></div><% } %>
    <% if (error) { %><div class="alert alert-error"><%= error %></div><% } %>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Current email</h2>
      <p><%= email %></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Change email address</h2>
      <form method="POST" action="/settings/update-email">
        <label>New email</label>
        <input type="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Update email</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <div class="card note-card">
      <strong>Lab note:</strong> this application also accepts email changes through
      a plain GET request at <code>/settings/update-email?email=...</code> with no
      additional checks. That is the vulnerability this lab demonstrates.
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
